--TEST--
A helper's fault is raised with no site of its own, so the frame it happened in is recorded where nothing else would record one: the catchable edge of the landing site — `rule:errors/throw-is-not-slower`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every other label in a backtrace is pushed by a frame the exception *leaves*,
// and a `throw` renders its own from the site it was compiled with. A helper
// raising its own fault does neither, and a `catch` in the frame that called
// the helper unwinds out of nothing — so without a seed on that one edge the
// exception reaches the handler naming nowhere.
class Relay {
    // The clause here matches nothing, so the same object is handed onward.
    public static function narrow(string $text): mixed {
        try {
            return Core\Json::decode($text);
        } catch (IOError $io) {
            return 0;
        }
    }
}

try {
    var $bad = Core\Json::decode("{");
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "in-frame=", $e->location, "\n";
    foreach ($e->backtrace as string $frame) {
        echo "  ", $frame, "\n";
    }
}

// The seeded frame is provisional, exactly as a `throw`'s own is: the label the
// frame pushes on its way out replaces it rather than naming the frame twice.
try {
    var $onward = Relay::narrow("{");
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "onward=", $e->location, "\n";
    foreach ($e->backtrace as string $frame) {
        echo "  ", $frame, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
in-frame=case.nvs:19
  <script>() at case.nvs:19
onward=case.nvs:11
  Relay::narrow() at case.nvs:13
